<edge source="iran_us_standoff::chokepoint_export_vol" target="alliance_security_realig::armed_conflict_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp declines in crude transits through key chokepoints prompt affected producer and consumer states to use military means (escorts, interdictions, strikes) to reopen or secure routes, producing new or intensified kinetic operations in the maritime and littoral battlespace.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_us_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">alliance_security_realig</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_us_standoff::chokepoint_export_vol" target="global_bond_credit_stres::cross_border_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A drop in crude exports through key chokepoints cuts export receipts for producing countries and triggers sudden stops or reversals in capital flows as FX revenues and sovereign/NGP flows decline.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_us_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_credit_stres</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_us_standoff::chokepoint_export_vol" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_stress" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">A fall in crude flow through key chokepoints reduces feedstock availability for refiners and cuts exportable refined products to Europe, directly tightening diesel and jet‑fuel availability for Ukrainian military and civilian needs and raising energy supply stress; conversely restoration of volumes eases that stress.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_us_standoff</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
